    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm seeing a CrashLoopBackOff on our auth-service in the prod gke cluster. logs are pretty sparse but i'm seeing some exit code 137s. can u give me a diagnostic checklist to figure out if this is a memory issue, a liveness probe thing, or something else?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A `CrashLoopBackOff` with exit code 137 in GKE usually signals that your container is being killed by the OOM (Out Of Memory) killer.  First, check your Pod's resource requests and limits, specifically the memory limits. If the application is consuming more than the limit, the kernel will terminate it with code 137. You might also want to check the Kubernetes events for the pod to see if OOMKilled is explicitly listed. If the memory limits look fine, then you might need to investigate the application's behavior under load, perhaps by temporarily increasing the memory limit for testing.",
      "source": "target",
